  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> is the line of intersection of the planes <math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is the line of intersection of the planes <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0,</mn></math>&nbsp;then the distance of the origin from the plane, containing the lines <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is",
